// RUN: split-file %s %t
//
// The ten analysis-negative inputs first parse and verify as ordinary CIR.
// Missing targets separately exercise their preexisting native-verifier error. Use text/bytecode without canonicalization,
// which could intentionally erase unreachable invalid constructs.
// ERROR: error: unsupported {{(control flow|CFG terminator)}} in lifetime analysis
//
// Duplicate/argument/indirect/inward/sibling controls have no switch. The
// first three expose missing validation; inward/sibling already fail after
// analysis and remain rejected. Symbol checks must not depend on hasSwitch.
// Duplicate and argument-taking labels are deliberately unreferenced.
// A sibling if region shares its parent operation with the source region; that
// does not make it an ancestor. The nonlinear shell guards isSimpleForm's
// first-block-only check. Existing lifetime-parallel-failure.cir separately
// preserves function-local successor failure and other functions' diagnostics.

// Missing targets are already rejected by FuncOp verification. This is a
// native-verifier compatibility control, not a new lifetime-validation RED.
// MISSING: error: 'cir.func' op goto/label mismatch
// RUN: not cir-opt %t/missing.cir -o /dev/null 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MISSING

// duplicate
// RUN: cir-opt %t/duplicate.cir --mlir-print-debuginfo -o %t/duplicate.text.cir
// RUN: cir-opt %t/duplicate.cir --emit-bytecode -o %t/duplicate.bc
// RUN: not cir-opt %t/duplicate.cir --mlir-disable-threading=true --cir-lifetime-check="history=all" -o /dev/null 2> %t/duplicate.serial
// RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ERROR --input-file=%t/duplicate.serial --implicit-check-not='error:' --implicit-check-not='warning:' --implicit-check-not='remark:' --implicit-check-not='note:'
